### ============================================================
### POS KopiTiam - VS Code REST Client API Testing
### Refactored: 3 Roles, Normalized Payments, M2M Categories
### ============================================================
### Cara pakai:
### 1. Install extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client)
### 2. Buka file ini di VS Code
### 3. Klik "Send Request" di atas setiap block
### 4. Variable otomatis tersimpan antar request
### ============================================================
### NOTE: Jalankan dalam urutan yang ditentukan!
### Seed credentials (3 core roles only):
###   manager@kopitiam.id  / password123 / PIN 111111
###   cashier@kopitiam.id  / password123 / PIN 222222
###   kitchen@kopitiam.id  / password123 / PIN 333333
### ============================================================


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### PHASE 1: HEALTH & AUTH
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1.1 Health Check
# @name healthCheck
GET http://localhost:8080/health


### 1.2 Login Manager (email + password)
# @name loginManager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@kopitiam.id",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 1.3 Login Cashier (email + password)
# @name loginCashierEmail
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "cashier@kopitiam.id",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 1.4 Login Cashier (PIN – quick login at terminal)
# @name loginCashier
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login-pin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pin": "222222"
}

### 1.5 Login Kitchen (PIN)
# @name loginKitchen
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login-pin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pin": "333333"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### PHASE 2: MENUS (Many-to-Many categories)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2.1 Get Active Menus
### Response includes "categories" array (M2M) instead of single category_id
# @name getMenus
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/menus
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.data.access_token}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### PHASE 3: ORDERS (Dine In) — Full lifecycle
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### NOTE: Totals (subtotal, tax_amount, service_charge, total) are calculated
###       server-side by CalculateOrderTotals(). Do NOT send them in the request.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3.1 Create Order (Dine In)
# @name createOrderDineIn
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "table_id": "",
  "customer_id": "",
  "order_type": "dine_in",
  "notes": "Less sugar, extra ice",
  "discount_amount": 0,
  "items": [
    {
      "menu_id": "{{getMenus.response.body.data[0].id}}",
      "menu_name": "{{getMenus.response.body.data[0].name}}",
      "quantity": 2,
      "price": {{getMenus.response.body.data[0].price}},
      "notes": "Hot"
    },
    {
      "menu_id": "{{getMenus.response.body.data[4].id}}",
      "menu_name": "{{getMenus.response.body.data[4].name}}",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": {{getMenus.response.body.data[4].price}},
      "notes": ""
    }
  ]
}

### 3.2 Get All Orders
# @name getAllOrders
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 3.3 Get Order by ID
# @name getOrderById
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 3.4 Get Order by Number
# @name getOrderByNumber
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/by-number/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.order_number}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 3.5 Confirm Order (Deduct stock — branches on Menu.is_recipe_based)
# @name confirmOrder
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 3.6 Update Order Notes
# @name updateOrder
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Customer requests extra napkins"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### PHASE 4: PAYMENT (Normalized — Split-based)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Payment model is normalized: the Payment header now only stores
### change_amount and status. Per-method details live in the splits array.
###
### Endpoint: POST /api/v1/payments?order_id={order_id}
### Payload:
###   - change_amount: float
###   - splits: array of { payment_method, amount, reference_number? }
###
### Supported payment_method values:
###   cash | qris | debit_card | credit_card | transfer | e_wallet
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4.1 Process Payment — Full Cash (Single Method)
# @name paymentCash
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments?order_id={{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "change_amount": 29070,
  "splits": [
    {
      "payment_method": "cash",
      "amount": 100000
    }
  ]
}

### 4.2 Process Payment — QRIS (Cashless)
# @name paymentQRIS
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments?order_id={{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "change_amount": 0,
  "splits": [
    {
      "payment_method": "qris",
      "amount": 70930,
      "reference_number": "QRIS-20260514-001"
    }
  ]
}

### 4.3 Process Payment — Split (Cash + QRIS)
### Customer pays part cash, part QRIS
# @name paymentSplit
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments?order_id={{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "change_amount": 0,
  "splits": [
    {
      "payment_method": "cash",
      "amount": 50000
    },
    {
      "payment_method": "qris",
      "amount": 20930,
      "reference_number": "QRIS-20260514-002"
    }
  ]
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### PHASE 5: ORDERS (Takeaway — for Cancel/Void tests)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5.1 Create Order (Takeaway)
# @name createOrderTakeaway
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "table_id": "",
  "customer_id": "",
  "order_type": "takeaway",
  "notes": "Packaging separate",
  "discount_amount": 5000,
  "items": [
    {
      "menu_id": "{{getMenus.response.body.data[1].id}}",
      "menu_name": "{{getMenus.response.body.data[1].name}}",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": {{getMenus.response.body.data[1].price}},
      "notes": ""
    }
  ]
}

### 5.2 Cancel Order (Cashier can cancel pending orders)
# @name cancelOrder
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/{{createOrderTakeaway.response.body.data.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 5.3 Void Order (Manager Only)
# @name voidOrder
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/{{createOrderTakeaway.response.body.data.id}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Customer walked away before pickup"
}

### 5.4 Void Line Item (Manager Only)
# @name voidItem
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}/void-item
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order_detail_id": "{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.order_details[0].id}}",
  "reason": "Customer changed mind"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### PHASE 6: RETURNS (Harus setelah order confirmed)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6.1 Process Return (Cashier or Manager)
# @name processReturn
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/returns?order_id={{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}&processed_by={{loginCashier.response.body.data.user.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "return_amount": 18000,
  "reason": "Wrong order — customer wanted tea not coffee"
}


