### 12.1 Generate Receipt Payload (Cashier)
# @name generateReceipt
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/printer/receipt/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCashier.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 12.2 Generate Kitchen Ticket (Kitchen)
# @name generateKitchenTicket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/printer/kitchen-ticket/{{createOrderDineIn.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginKitchen.response.body.data.access_token}}


### ============================================================
### TESTING SCENARIOS
### ============================================================
###
### SCENARIO A: Full Order Lifecycle (Dine In + Cash Payment)
###   1.1 → 1.2 → 2.1 → 3.1 → 3.5 → 4.1 → 12.1 → 12.2
###   Result: Order created → confirmed (stock deducted) → paid → receipt
###
### SCENARIO B: Split Payment
###   1.2 → 2.1 → 3.1 → 3.5 → 4.3 → 12.1
###   Result: Order paid via Cash + QRIS split
###
### SCENARIO C: Cancel / Void
###   1.2 → 2.1 → 5.1 → 5.2  (cancel by cashier)
###   1.2 → 2.1 → 5.1 → 5.3  (void by manager)
###
### SCENARIO D: Return after Confirmed Order
###   (after SCENARIO A) → 6.1
###   Result: Partial refund processed
###
### SCENARIO E: Shift Management
###   1.4 → 7.1 → 7.2 → 7.3
###   Result: Shift opened, inspected, closed with variance
###
### SCENARIO F: Inventory & BOM (Recipe-based menu)
###   1.2 → 8.1 → 9.1 → 9.2 → 9.3 → 9.4 → 8.4
###   Result: Raw material + Recipe CRUD; ConfirmOrder will use
###           pessimistic locking to deduct raw materials.
###
### SCENARIO G: Employee CRUD
###   1.2 → 10.1 → 10.2 → 10.3 → 10.4
###   Roles: manager | cashier | kitchen  (superadmin removed)
###
### ============================================================
